# delay_buftree — fanout-limited buffer tree (no dnsize collapse).
#
# Most other delay/area recipes end with `buffer; topo; upsize {D}; dnsize
# {D};`. On designs with a handful of very-high-fanout nets (e.g. the
# SRAM write-enable in a flat MCU netlist) the trailing `dnsize {D}` is
# greedy enough to collapse the buffer tree back to a single `clkbuf_1`
# driving 40+ sinks, producing 10+ ns of wire-load tail at SS corner
# even though the underlying logic is clean.
#
# This recipe drops `dnsize` and runs two `buffer -N 16; topo; upsize {D};`
# iterations after the GIA mapper. Cost: ~+8% cells, ~+20% area on large
# designs. Benefit on the nc_mcu nc_lib reference: SS setup WNS improved
# from -24.6 ns to -8.8 ns (~+60% Fmax at SS).

strash; ifraig; scorr; dc2; dc2; dretime; strash;
balance; rewrite; refactor; balance; rewrite;
&get -n; &st; &dch; &nf {D}; &put;
buffer -N 16; topo; upsize {D}; buffer -N 16; topo; upsize {D};
stime
